{"author":{"id":"40e3ba2788b3b9fc163c354afc44e5f9d225bcf0a27e679aaa878dd6135c6dcb"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1777935630,"nonce":"Ai4mua+XmIuothTbRZhYtiqQyzw=","message":"Cross-compile pipeline lands on main: cmake/djgpp-toolchain.cmake + cmake/README-djgpp.md.\n\nVerified against the DJGPP prebuilt toolchain from andrewwutw/build-djgpp v3.4 (gcc 12.2.0); also tested with the gcc 7.2.0 build from djfdyuruiry/djgpp docker image.\n\nlibuc2 (all 14 sources including new uc2_ingest.c) compiles clean.  CLI compiles via the existing cli/src/compat/compat_dos.c shim (already authored for this purpose).  Output is a 359 KB MZ+COFF+go32 DOS executable.\n\nNotable gotcha documented in cmake/README-djgpp.md: the cross-gcc respects CPATH/CPLUS_INCLUDE_PATH from the build shell regardless of -nostdinc, so any host include directory exported there ends up first in the search path -- a session that had Intel oneAPI sourced was the immediate failure mode.  Remediation is 'unset CPATH' or 'env -u CPATH cmake'.\n\nClosing this issue.  Follow-ups (DOSBox-X smoke test + CI matrix entry) tracked separately as P2.","files":null}]}